on 53X PacBio data and 193X Arima Hi-C data generated as part of the ATLASea programme (https:\/\/www.atlasea.fr). The assembly process included the following steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm, removal of contaminant sequences using Context, removal of haplotypic duplications using purge_dups, and Hi-C-based scaffolding with YaHS. In total, 135 contigs were identified as contaminants (bacterial, archaeal, or viral), totaling 10.816 Mb (with the largest being 2.521 Mb). Additionally, 1123 regions totaling 23.834 Mb (with the largest being 0.576 Mb) were identified as haplotypic duplications and removed. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using OATK. Finally, the primary assembly was analyzed and manually improved using Pretext. During manual curation, 16 haplotypic regions and 4267 contaminant sequences were removed, totaling 17.08Mb and 163Mb, respectively (with the largest being 7.16Mb and 0.445Mb). Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by Hi-C data were named in order of size. Many contaminant sequences assigned to a Dinophyceae species. Those sequences were removed before performing the manual curation."},"assembly_stats":{"total_number_of_chromosomes":16,"total_sequence_length":"478188328","total_ungapped_length":"478179428","number_of_contigs":213,"contig_n50":10116134,"contig_l50":13,"number_of_scaffolds":154,"scaffold_n50":31630632,"scaffold_l50":4,"number_of_component_sequences":154,"atgc_count":"478179428","gc_count":"178266629","gc_percent":37.5,"genome_coverage":"53","number_of_organelles":1},"organelle_info":[{"description":"Mitochondrion","total_seq_length":"18547","submitter":"Genoscope"}],"wgs_info":{"wgs_project_accession":"CEVNFB01","master_wgs_url":"https:\/\/www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\/nuccore\/CEVNFB000000000.1","wgs_contigs_url":"https:\/\/www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\/Traces\/wgs\/CEVNFB01"}}]}